<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 06-FEB.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 06-FEB.</headline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Cyclone Pancho-Helinda, with 40 mph winds, is in the southern Indian Ocean near 20s/84e, moving southwest at 7 mph. It is expected to rapidly weaken and dissipate by 12-24 hours. This system will remain a moderate risk to shipping during this time.  </p>
<p>There are no further statements at this time.</p>
</text>
